  "title": "An Exercise in Data Analysis: MoTrPAC at the American Society of Human Genetics",
  "bodyHtml": "<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);font-family:Arial, sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:normal;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-variant-emoji:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-position:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">At the American Society of Human Genetics (ASHG) 2024 Annual Meeting,&nbsp;</span><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);color:rgb(0, 0, 0);font-family:Arial, sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:normal;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-variant-emoji:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-position:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">The Molecular Transducers of Physical Activity Consortium&nbsp;</span><a style=\"text-decoration:none;\" href=\"https://www.motrpac.org/\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(17, 85, 204);font-family:Arial, sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:normal;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-variant-emoji:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-position:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><u>(MoTrPAC)</u></span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);font-family:Arial, sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:normal;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-variant-emoji:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-position:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\"> hosted an interactive ASHG Ancillary Session, entitled, “MoTrPAC Data Hub: A Hands-On Experience Exploring the Molecular Map of Exercise.” The session kicked off with a program overview by MoTrPAC Bioinformatician and Software Engineer Mihir Samdarshi, followed by an interactive R tutorial from MoTrPAC Bioinformatics Lead David Jimenez-Morales. Users performed hands-on data analysis of multi-tissue and multi-assay MoTrPAC datasets acquired across four training time points in young adult male and female rats exposed to an 8-week endurance exercise program and sedentary controls.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);color:rgb(0, 0, 0);font-family:Arial, sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:normal;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-variant-emoji:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-position:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">All data from the landmark study on endurance exercise training in young adult rats are now available at the&nbsp;</span><a style=\"text-decoration:none;\" href=\"https://motrpac-data.org/\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);color:rgb(17, 85, 204);font-family:Arial, sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:normal;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-variant-emoji:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-position:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><u>MoTrPAC Data Hub</u></span></a><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);color:rgb(0, 0, 0);font-family:Arial, sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:normal;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-variant-emoji:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-position:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">. This comprehensive dataset provides a detailed molecular and physiological map of the exercise response, contributing to MoTrPAC's efforts to characterize the molecular fingerprint of physical activity. The consortium is also conducting additional studies involving both human participants and animal models, with multi-omics, multi-tissue, and multi-species datasets from these ongoing studies to be released soon. For more information, please visit&nbsp;</span><a style=\"text-decoration:none;\" href=\"https://motrpac-data.org/project-overview\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);color:rgb(17, 85, 204);font-family:Arial, sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:normal;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-variant-emoji:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-position:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><u>this link</u></span></a><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);color:rgb(0, 0, 0);font-family:Arial, sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:normal;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-variant-emoji:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-position:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">.</span></p>",
  "summary": "MoTrPAC hosts a hands-on data analysis session for users to study the molecular effects of exercise.",
